Please see the Ardour website at https://ardour.org/ for all documentation.

For information on building Ardour:

https://ardour.org/development.html

## Change log

Implements Ableton-style per-clip warp markers for the Cue/Trigger system and AudioRegions. Each marker binds an audio sample position to a musical beat position; between adjacent markers, a local stretch ratio is computed and fed to RubberBandStretcher::setTimeRatio() per block, enabling non-uniform time-stretching that tracks session tempo map changes in real-time.

Backend (libs/ardour/)
WarpMarker / WarpMap — sorted (sample_pos, beat_pos) pairs with binary-search interpolation, per-segment stretch ratio math, and XML round-trip serialization:
// ratio = (beat_delta × session_spb) / sample_delta
double ratio = warp_map.stretch_ratio_at(beat_pos, sr * 60.0 / bpm);
stretcher->setTimeRatio(ratio);
WarpMode enum (Beats / Tones / Texture / Re-Pitch / Complex / ComplexPro) → RubberBandStretcher::Options mapping; Re-Pitch bypasses RubberBand entirely and changes the fractional read increment instead
ElasticStretcher — wraps RubberBandStretcher with WarpMap-driven per-segment ratios, Re-Pitch linear-interpolation path, loop crossfade buffer, and start-padding latency management
TransientAnalysisCache — async TransientDetector runs on a detached std::thread; uses shared_ptr<atomic<bool>> stop-flag so destruction never races with in-flight analysis; provides build_initial_warp_map() from detected onset positions
Modified existing files
triggerbox.h/cc: Trigger protected section + UIState gain _warp_enabled, _warp_mode, _warp_map; AudioTrigger gets _elastic_stretcher, warp setters, audio_run() branch, and get_state/set_state serialization. Warp is opt-in (_warp_enabled = false by default — zero overhead for existing sessions).
audioregion.h/cc: AudioRegion gains a WarpMap property persisted in region XML
UI (gtk2_ardour/)
WarpEditor — Cairo-based waveform overview with draggable orange marker triangles, beat grid overlay, transient tick marks, scroll-to-zoom, and right-click context menu (delete / snap-to-transient)
AudioTriggerPropertiesBox — new "Tempo Warp" frame with enable toggle, six-mode dropdown, and inline WarpEditor panel; syncs bidirectionally via the existing PropertyChanged / UIState mechanism
Backward compatibility
Sessions without <WarpMap> XML load normally. The legacy uniform-stretch path in audio_run() is completely unaffected when _warp_enabled is false.


## Building

```bash
./waf clean
./waf configure --strict --optimize --cxx17 --prefix=/opt/ardour   --with-backends=alsa,pulseaudio --lv2 --vst3 2>&1 | tee configure.log

./waf -j1 2>&1 | tee build.log
```

## Running

```bash
TOP=..
libs=$TOP/build/libs

export LD_LIBRARY_PATH="$libs/tk/ydk-pixbuf:$libs/tk/ztk:$libs/tk/ydk:$libs/tk/ytk:$libs/tk/ztkmm:$libs/tk/ydkmm:$libs/tk/ytkmm:$libs/tk/suil:$libs/ptformat:$libs/qm-dsp:$libs/vamp-sdk:$libs/surfaces:$libs/ctrl-interface/control_protocol:$libs/ctrl-interface/midi_surface:$libs/ardour:$libs/midi++2:$libs/pbd:$libs/rubberband:$libs/soundtouch:$libs/aaf:$libs/gtkmm2ext:$libs/widgets:$libs/appleutility:$libs/taglib:$libs/evoral:$libs/evoral/src/libsmf:$libs/audiographer:$libs/temporal:$libs/libltc:$libs/canvas:$libs/waveview:$libs/ardouralsautil${LD_LIBRARY_PATH:+:$LD_LIBRARY_PATH}"

./build/gtk2_ardour/ardour-9.2.576
```

## TODO

- Make BPM selector in top banner click draggable to change session tempo. Requires refactor of existing tempo map code to support real-time changes and per-clip overrides.
- Add transient snap option to WarpEditor context menu. Requires UI refresh on transient analysis completion, and possibly a visual "pending" state for unsnapped markers.
- Implement WarpMode::Texture using RubberBandStretcher::OptionProcessRealTime and OptionUseAntiAliasFilter. Requires UI refresh to show texture mode in properties box, and testing to verify real-time performance with typical session sizes.
- Add keyboard shortcuts for adding/deleting warp markers, and for nudging selected markers left/right. Requires UI focus management to ensure shortcuts only apply when WarpEditor is active, and visual feedback for selected markers.
- Implement undo/redo for warp marker edits. Requires integration with Ardour's undo system, and careful state management to ensure consistent behavior across multiple edits and session reloads.
- Add support for MIDI clip warping using a similar marker system. Requires design of a MIDI-specific WarpMap that accounts for note positions and velocities, and integration with the existing MIDI editing workflow.
- Optimize stretch ratio calculations by caching results for recently used beat positions. Requires implementation of a small LRU cache within WarpMap, and benchmarking to ensure it provides a performance boost without excessive memory usage.
- Add visual indicators for stretch ratio changes in the WarpEditor, such as color-coding or a ratio graph overlay. Requires UI design work to determine the best way to represent this information without cluttering the interface.
- Implement support for non-destructive clip warping, allowing users to toggle between warped and original audio without losing edits. Requires changes to the audio processing pipeline to maintain both versions of the audio data, and UI elements to switch between them.
- Implement individual clip pitch-shifting independent of time-stretching, possibly as an additional WarpMode or as a separate property. Requires changes to the audio processing code to apply pitch shifts without affecting timing, and UI elements to control pitch shift amount.
- Add warping and pitch-shifting capabilities to the UI's clip properties panel, allowing users to apply these effects without needing to use the WarpEditor. Requires UI design work to integrate these controls into the existing properties panel, and changes to the underlying Trigger code to support applying these effects from the properties panel.
- The current implementation of the WarpEditor uses a custom Cairo-based widget. Consider refactoring this to use a more standard GTK widget with custom drawing, to improve integration with the rest of the UI and potentially simplify event handling. Requires redesign of the WarpEditor UI to fit within a standard widget, and changes to the drawing code to work within the new widget's framework.
- Add support for saving and loading warp marker presets, allowing users to apply common warping configurations across multiple clips or sessions. Requires implementation of a preset management system, including UI for saving/loading presets and integration with the existing XML serialization for WarpMaps.
- Make the clip waveform preview zoomable and scrollable within the WarpEditor, to allow for more precise marker placement. Requires implementation of zoom and scroll functionality within the WarpEditor, and changes to the drawing code to account for the current zoom/scroll state when rendering the waveform and markers.